The position probe is finished. Moving the compressed slots to far-out positions costs nothing at either seed, so positions are not why long documents lose accuracy. My prediction was that it would cost at least 3 points, and that prediction was wrong.

## Done this wake
- **Why I was woken:** the check flagged the last running cell (40 pages, seed 43) for low GPU use. It is not stuck: its log reached row 1,080 of 1,407 at the same time as its finished seed-42 twin did, so I left it running. I added a row to the known-issues table and filed a report on expmon, because its low-GPU rule was written for training jobs and misfires on evaluation jobs.
- **Four cells finished cleanly.** Every question was judged, no judge reply failed to parse, and fewer than 2% of answers hit the length cap. All four ran on the same code version.
- **Position probe (decided, provisional).** Each 10-page question's slots were moved to the positions its 40-page version uses. Scores are paired on the same 1,407 questions:

| seed | shifted vs normal, judge accuracy ↑ (pt, 95% CI) | questions won / lost | answers whose wording changed |
|---|---|---|---|
| 42 | −0.6 [−1.4, +0.3] | 16 / 24 | 207 of 1,407 |
| 43 | −0.1 [−0.8, +0.6] | 11 / 13 | 194 of 1,407 |

  Both intervals sit inside ±3 points, which is the "not this cause" bar. About 200 answers changed wording, so the shift was really applied, but almost none changed from right to wrong.
- **Slot-reading probe, seed 42 complete.** This probe keeps only the eighth of the compressed slots (`<MEM>` tokens) that the model attends to most:
  - At 40 pages it gains +2.5 points over using all slots.
  - At 10 pages it changes nothing (−0.4).
  - The difference between the two, which is the test score, is **+2.8 [+0.4, +5.3]**. That is just under the 3-point bar for "a cause", but too far from zero to rule it out.
  - At seed 43 the 10-page half is +0.5; the 40-page half is still running.
- **Last cell launched (96 of the 96 allowed):** a second scoring of the six new result files with a different judge prompt, set to start only after the running cell succeeds.
- Compute used: 97.5 of 114 GPU-hours. The findings document `docs/longdoc_diagnosis.md`, the state file and the experiment log are updated. I deleted a stale verifier alert whose issue the previous wake had already fixed.

## Next
The next wake comes when both jobs end (within 3 hours). It will:
- finish the slot-reading test at seed 43 and check both probes under the second judge prompt;
- write the ranked list of causes for you as one question in BLOCKED.md.

If the slot-reading effect lands just under the bar again at seed 43, the campaign rule calls that "promising". That allows one repeat on new questions, which needs cells beyond the 96 allowed. That request will be part of the same question.

Nothing needed from you now.
